# The official Nix release that .github/scripts/install-nix.sh installs on CI
# runners, and the SHA-256 of its installer tarball for each runner system.
# The script checks the downloaded tarball against these digests before it
# extracts or runs anything. It parses this file and never sources it.
#
# qsdev's CI pin catalog (internal/cigeneration/nix-release.env in the qsdev
# repository) is the only source of these pins. qsdev writes a byte-identical
# copy into each project as .github/nix-release.env, and `qsdev update`
# replaces it, local edits included, so change the catalog instead.
#
# qsdev's tool-pins workflow (scripts/bump-tool-pins.sh) moves the pins to a
# newer release once its tarballs have been published for at least 3 days.
# Each KEY line sits directly below a "# source:" line naming where it looks:
#   nix-release <owner>/<repo>  Nix's X.Y.Z tags on GitHub, taken once the
#                               binary tarballs are on releases.nixos.org
#                               (aged from that publication)
#   nix-sha256 <system>         the SHA-256 of nix-<NIX_VERSION>-<system>.tar.xz,
#                               refreshed from the release's published .sha256
#                               whenever NIX_VERSION moves; must follow it

# source: nix-release NixOS/nix
NIX_VERSION=2.34.8

# source: nix-sha256 x86_64-linux
NIX_SHA256_X86_64_LINUX=2c2e146b80834fe0ca201b51deeb939405b4f18e8d2071bf80b10f8123c50464

# source: nix-sha256 aarch64-linux
NIX_SHA256_AARCH64_LINUX=b4e565fe4db5c352547b8146488cab81db06be89301a4c67b081c76f1e457760

# source: nix-sha256 aarch64-darwin
NIX_SHA256_AARCH64_DARWIN=ae3b2b1a74b956110d14dd813bee80ea46626a51ddce28d142e0805379a34acf

# source: nix-sha256 x86_64-darwin
NIX_SHA256_X86_64_DARWIN=14d3af62d1c1755da7e048519a73baeab3e856cba766e53fca5ceec4e6fe67e2
